Subscribing or buying a publication whose author or publisher who
violates university discrimination policies, does not violate
university discrimination policy. Churches (often) discriminate on the
basis of religion. The Daughters of the American Revolution
discriminated on the basis of national origin. The United States
Department of Defense discriminates on the basis of sexual preference.
All these organizations publish material that the university can, does
(and in my opinion should) buy.

What my university (as an example) can't do is:
  + help enforce such discrimination
  + give a discriminatory organization status as a registered student
      organization (RSO). RSO's get much easier access to university
      resources compared to other organizations.

- Carl

