If you were continually mailing 10M of mail, and refused to stop, then
presumably you are creating an immediate threat to a system (or several
systems) that can not handle the load.  If a reasonable argument could be
made that the case represents an "emergency" then he could immediately
suspend your account in order to alleviate the emergency.

(This differs from, say, forging a usenet header which, though prohibited,
can't be considered to be an "emergency.")


>>don't believe is that university staff (e.g. sys admin) have authority
>>to judge and discipline a user after the rule breaking has stopped.
